            <title>[LU-21156] replace rbtree for committing transaction with a simple array</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21156</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;on new kernels ext4 doesn't maintain a list committed transactions, so a new mechanism was introduced in &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19142" title="Restore ldiskfs transaction handling" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19142"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19142&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; - it uses an rbtree to maintain a collection of transactions with corresponding list of callbacks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I think this approach has few drawbacks:&lt;br/&gt;
1) there are only two transactions at any point in ext4: running and committing, using rbtree for 2 items seems a bit overuse.&lt;br/&gt;
2) each osd_thandle now has 24 bytes rb_node struct, but only one per ext4 transaction is used while we have hundreds or thousands of osd_thandle per ext4 transaction&lt;br/&gt;
3) a single spinlock is used to register a callback and to run a callback - we actually don't need spinlock to run callbacks&lt;/p&gt;</description>
